# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Design intentions {#design-intentions}"
msgstr "Mga layunin ng disenyo {#design-intentions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package is deliberately designed to align with Qiskit: it builds on a core implemented in Rust and provides first-party language bindings to Python and C. Its API intends to draw parallels to Qiskit in order to seamlessly integrate into the workflows of users with experience in programming Qiskit.\n"
msgstr "Sadyang dinisenyo ang package na ito para umayon sa Qiskit: nakabatay ito sa core na ipinatupad sa Rust at nagbibigay ng first-party na language binding para sa Python at C. Layunin ng API nito na tumulad sa Qiskit para maisama nang maayos sa workflow ng mga user na may karanasan sa pagprograma ng Qiskit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A core principle to the design of `qiskit-fermions` was the decoupling of its fermionic circuit representation from its qubitized form. To be more precise: the fermionic circuits are meaningful by themselves and do not require a mapping to qubit space to be interpretable. Furthermore, the fermionic circuit representation cannot make any assumptions about its fermion-to-qubit encoding applied later on. Consequently, while Jordan-Wigner retains a dominant position and role, it is not assumed to be the \\_default\\_ fermion-to-qubit encoding.\n"
msgstr "Isang pangunahing prinsipyo sa disenyo ng `qiskit-fermions` ang paghihiwalay ng fermionic circuit representation nito mula sa qubitized na anyo nito. Para maging mas tiyak: may sariling kahulugan ang mga fermionic circuit at hindi nangangailangan ng mapping sa qubit space para maunawaan. Higit pa rito, hindi maaaring gumawa ang fermionic circuit representation ng anumang pagpapalagay tungkol sa fermion-to-qubit encoding na ilalapat sa huli. Dahil dito, bagama't nananatiling nangingibabaw ang posisyon at papel ng Jordan-Wigner, hindi ito ipinapalagay na ang \\_default\\_ na fermion-to-qubit encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Relationship to ffsim {#relationship-to-ffsim}"
msgstr "Relasyon sa ffsim {#relationship-to-ffsim}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) and `qiskit-fermions` divide the work rather than overlap. ffsim owns the high-level ansatz operators and their fast simulation: it constructs a UCJ or UCCSD operator from coupled-cluster amplitudes or a parameter vector, and simulates fermionic states in a compact fixed-particle-number space. `qiskit-fermions` owns the circuit side: it expresses that operator as a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") on fermionic modes and transpiles it into a qubit circuit through *any* fermion-to-qubit encoding.\n"
msgstr "Naghahati ng trabaho ang [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) at `qiskit-fermions` sa halip na magpatong. Hawak ng ffsim ang mga high-level na ansatz operator at ang mabilis na simulation ng mga ito: bumubuo ito ng UCJ o UCCSD operator mula sa coupled-cluster amplitude o parameter vector, at nagsi-simulate ng mga fermionic state sa compact na fixed-particle-number space. Hawak ng `qiskit-fermions` ang bahagi ng circuit: ipinapahayag nito ang operator na iyon bilang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") sa mga fermionic mode at tina-transpile ito sa isang qubit circuit sa pamamagitan ng *anumang* fermion-to-qubit encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That last point is the reason to bring an ffsim operator here. ffsim’s own Qiskit gates are specific to the Jordan-Wigner transformation, so lowering an ansatz through a different encoding (a local encoding trading qubits for shallower circuits, for instance) is what this package adds. Conversely, this package does not reimplement the ansatz math, so [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") and [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") take an ffsim operator directly as their input.\n"
msgstr "Iyan ang dahilan para dalhin dito ang isang ffsim operator. Partikular sa Jordan-Wigner transformation ang sariling mga Qiskit gate ng ffsim, kaya ang pag-lower ng ansatz gamit ang ibang encoding (halimbawa, isang local encoding na ipinagpapalit ang mga qubit para sa mas mababaw na circuit) ang idinaragdag ng package na ito. Sa kabilang banda, hindi nire-reimplement ng package na ito ang ansatz math, kaya direktang tumatanggap ng ffsim operator bilang input ang [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") at [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On the simulation side, ffsim is the backend. This package’s gates and operators implement the protocol methods ffsim’s simulation functions consume (`_apply_unitary_`, `_linear_operator_` and `_trace_`; see [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\")), so ffsim’s tools work on them natively, with no conversion step. Building operators, mapping them and transpiling the resulting circuits do not need ffsim at all.\n"
msgstr "Sa panig ng simulation, ang ffsim ang backend. Ipinapatupad ng mga gate at operator ng package na ito ang mga protocol method na ginagamit ng mga simulation function ng ffsim (`_apply_unitary_`, `_linear_operator_` at `_trace_`; tingnan ang [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\")), kaya natural na gumagana sa mga ito ang mga tool ng ffsim, nang walang hakbang ng conversion. Hindi na kailangan ng ffsim sa pagbuo ng mga operator, pag-map ng mga ito at pag-transpile ng mga resultang circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the full picture, read the [ffsim relationship guide](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Para sa buong larawan, basahin ang [ffsim relationship guide](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation).\n"

